From 76688fa58162f273abac728dde4b416d07a9e61d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 13:37:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 37/75] wm: flag dialog tasks by root activity, not top (ARC)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Task.setTaskMetadata() set METADATA_IS_DIALOG when the *top* activity used a
floating theme. The Chrome-side fydroid composer turns a dialog task into a
frameless modal overlay, so this flagged a normal app the instant it showed a
dialog-themed activity on top: the metadata propagates to the task's child
layers and the composer latches the whole app task into a modal. Worse,
setTaskMetadata re-runs from makeAnimationLeash (the dialog-open transition),
so the flag flips mid-animation and — because the composer never reverts a
latched modal — the app stays collapsed into a dialog.

Check the ROOT activity instead: a task is a dialog only when it is
fundamentally a standalone dialog (PackageInstaller, permission prompts, whose
base activity is floating). An app showing a dialog activity on top keeps its
normal app root, so it is no longer misclassified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: If84134c5830826ec54afc3ea5ff0cd968b717ee1
---
 services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
index 08504a575201..2166eade3dca 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
@@ -3119,7 +3119,15 @@ class Task extends TaskFragment {
                         == ApplicationInfo.CATEGORY_GAME) {
             b.setMetadata(METADATA_IS_GAME, 1);
         }
-        if (isDialogTask(topActivity)) {
+        // A task is a dialog task only when its ROOT activity uses a floating
+        // theme — i.e. the whole task is a standalone dialog (PackageInstaller,
+        // permission prompts). Checking the top activity instead flags a normal
+        // app the moment it shows a dialog-themed activity on top: the task
+        // metadata propagates to all child layers, and the Chrome-side composer
+        // latches the entire app task into a modal overlay. setTaskMetadata is
+        // re-run on makeAnimationLeash (the dialog-open transition), so the
+        // top-activity check would flip mid-animation and stick.
+        if (isDialogTask(getRootActivity())) {
             b.setMetadata(METADATA_IS_DIALOG, 1);
         }
         if (getActivityType() == ACTIVITY_TYPE_HOME) {
